  outline: none;
  box-shadow: 0 0 5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
}

button {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 10px;
  background-color: #4CAF50;
  color: white;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 5px;
  cursor: pointer;
}

button:hover {
  background-color: #45a049;
}
```

This CSS will style the form with a light gray background, rounded borders, and a light gray input field with rounded borders. The input fields will have a padding of 10px and a margin of 10px between them. The submit button will have a green background and white text, with rounded borders and a hover effect. The form will be centered on the page with a maximum width of 400px.

You can customize the CSS to fit the design of your website. For example, you can change the background color, font family, and padding of the input fields to match the design of your website. You can also add more styles to the form, such as a label for each input field, or a placeholder text for the input fields.

